subproblem.statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ, let μ_j (j ∈ ℕ) and μ be measures on the Borel sets of ℝ^P (Measure (Euclid P)), and let ρ > 0. Assume:
(H2) μ(B_r(0)) < ∞ for every r > 0;
(H3) for every r > 0, μ_j(B_r(0)) < ∞ for all sufficiently large j;
(H4) ∫ f dμ_j → ∫ f dμ (Bochner integrals) for every continuous f : ℝ^P → ℝ with compact support;
(H5) μ(sphere(0, ρ)) = 0, where sphere(0, ρ) = {y : |y| = ρ} = ∂B_ρ(0).
Then μ_j(B_ρ(0)) → μ(B_ρ(0)) in [0, ∞].
